      "step": "mechanism",
      "text": "Vasospastic angina involves impaired coronary vasomotion (physiological rhythmic contractions) in one or more coronary arteries, with vascular smooth-muscle-cell dysfunction coupled with a predominance of vasoconstrictive metabolites playing an additional role; a localised vasomotion abnormality may cause focal (segmental) spasm in a coronary artery, while a more diffuse abnormality may cause multivessel spasm.",
