      "topic": "Atrial fibrillation",
      "step": "risk factors",
      "text": "Anyone can develop atrial fibrillation, but it may be more likely in people aged 55 or older, men, people living with obesity or overweight, smokers, people taking certain medicines such as levothyroxine, lithium or asthma medicines such as salbutamol, and people doing endurance sports such as long-distance running, cycling or skiing.",
