      "topic": "Atrial flutter",
      "step": "mechanism",
      "text": "In typical atrial flutter, the direction of depolarisation defines counterclockwise flutter when the wavefront crosses the cavotricuspid isthmus, ascends the septal wall and descends the anterolateral right atrial wall; the opposite, less common direction is clockwise or reverse flutter.",
