      "text": "Symptoms of heart failure include feeling out of breath when doing everyday activities or lying down; being more out of breath than expected when doing physical activity; feeling weak, light-headed or very tired, particularly after moving or doing physical activity; feeling light-headed or dizzy; swelling in the feet, ankles, legs or tummy, or feeling bloated; sudden weight gain; coughing at night; and coughing up frothy pink phlegm.",
