      "topic": "Heart failure",
      "step": "management",
      "text": "The NHS emergency advice for heart failure is to call 999 for severe breathing difficulty with gasping or choking or inability to speak, pale or blue or grey lips or skin that may be easier to see on palms or soles or gums in brown or black skin, or someone who has passed out and is not responding normally; do not drive yourself to A&E, and the person answering 999 will advise what to do.",
