      "topic": "Heart failure",
      "step": "management",
      "text": "For heart failure symptoms, different medicines may be given to increase urination and reduce fluid build-up, such as the diuretic furosemide; widen blood vessels so the heart does less work pumping, such as candesartan or enalapril; and slow the heart so it needs less oxygen, such as beta blockers.",
