      "topic": "Heart failure",
      "step": "management",
      "text": "The NHS urgent advice in heart failure is to request an urgent GP appointment or help from NHS 111 if breathlessness occurs lying down or during everyday activity, frothy pink phlegm is coughed up, or weight has suddenly increased; NHS 111 can be contacted by phone or online.",
