      "topic": "Heart failure",
      "step": "mechanism",
      "text": "Although preserved-ejection-fraction heart failure likely has multifactorial pathophysiology, reduced-ejection-fraction heart failure has a central imbalance of cardiovascular neuroendocrine systems: sympathetic and renin–angiotensin–aldosterone activation is not adequately opposed by increased natriuretic-peptide release, promoting progressive chamber hypertrophy and dilatation that impair pumping, cause symptoms and increase susceptibility to arrhythmias and conduction disorders.",
