      "topic": "Heart failure",
      "step": "mechanism",
      "text": "BNP is produced primarily by ventricular cardiomyocytes in response to volume or pressure overload; circulating BNP and NT-proBNP are normally very low but increase significantly in heart failure as a mechanism to restore normal haemodynamics.",
