      "topic": "Hypertension",
      "step": "prognosis",
      "text": "The Blood Pressure Lowering Treatment Trialists' Collaboration reported that the reduction in major adverse cardiovascular events was proportional to the size of the fall in systolic blood pressure, down to at least 120 mmHg in people aged under 75, with and without previous cardiovascular disease; overall, events were reduced by 10% for each 5 mmHg reduction in systolic blood pressure, with a greater effect in younger people (aged under 55: hazard ratio 0.82, 95% confidence interval 0.76 to 0.88) than in older people (aged 65 to 74: hazard ratio 0.91, 95% confidence interval 0.87 to 0.96).",
