      "topic": "Hypertension",
      "step": "risk factors",
      "text": "Therapeutic agents and other substances that may affect blood pressure include cocaine, stimulants often used for ADHD, narcolepsy and hypersomnias, decongestants, bronchodilators and antidepressants (sympathetic activation); NSAIDs, sex hormones such as the combined contraceptive pill, corticosteroids, liquorice and sodium-containing antacids (volume retention); VEGF inhibitors and calcineurin inhibitors (direct vasoconstriction); and erythrocyte stimulating agents, tyrosine kinase inhibitors and diet supplements such as ephedra, yohimbine and bitter orange (other mechanisms).",
