      "topic": "Hypertension",
      "step": "risk factors",
      "text": "The chance of having high blood pressure is increased by older age, having close relatives with high blood pressure, a Black African, Black Caribbean or South Asian ethnic background, an unhealthy diet (especially one high in salt), being overweight, smoking, drinking too much alcohol and feeling stressed over a long period.",
