      "topic": "Hypertension",
      "step": "risk factors",
      "text": "Among people with young-onset hypertension, coarctation of the aorta, phaeochromocytoma, Cushing's syndrome and thyroid disease are rare, with a prevalence of 1% or less, whereas up to 10% may have primary hyperaldosteronism, renal artery stenosis (more commonly fibromuscular dysplasia, Takayasu arteritis or neurofibromatosis than atherosclerosis) or renal parenchymal disease.",
