      "topic": "Hypertension",
      "step": "risk factors",
      "text": "Primary aldosteronism is the most common endocrine cause of secondary hypertension, with a prevalence of 2 to 6% among people with hypertension; screening should be considered in adults under 40, and where there is spontaneous or thiazide-induced hypokalaemia (serum potassium below 3.5 mmol/L), resistant hypertension, a family history or an adrenal incidentaloma found on imaging.",
