      "topic": "Hypertension",
      "step": "risk factors",
      "text": "Secondary hypertension has an identifiable underlying cause or precipitating factor; it accounts for 5 to 10% of cases and may be suggested by abnormal findings when assessing for target organ damage, or by specific clinical features including characteristic symptoms, signs or demographic factors.",
