      "topic": "Pericarditis",
      "step": "clinical features",
      "text": "The main symptom of pericarditis is chest pain. It usually feels sharp or stabbing, spreads to the shoulders, arms or tummy, worsens with deep breaths, swallowing, coughing or lying down, especially on the left side, and improves on leaning forward.",
