      "text": "A nationwide Japanese cohort of 20,000 hospitalised patients with pericarditis examined rates of cardiac tamponade in autoimmune pericarditis. In patients with autoimmune pericarditis, systemic lupus erythematosus was the diagnosis most commonly associated with tamponade, followed by rheumatoid arthritis and systemic sclerosis.",
