      "text": "A person with lupus might also have headaches; mouth ulcers; a high temperature; hair loss; weight loss; swollen glands, usually in the neck, armpits or groin; depression and anxiety; chest or tummy pain; or Raynaud's (changes in the colour of the fingers and toes when cold, anxious or stressed).",
